// cluster.proto — dashcenter.v1.ClusterService
//
// Returns a fleet-topology snapshot: who runs the controller cluster,
// where do they listen, which DPUs do they manage, what's the leader,
// what's healthy. Read-only; runs on any node (leader OR follower).
//
// Design: docs/dashd-features/cluster-topology-design.md
//
// Membership semantics
// --------------------
// Each dashd process publishes its own PeerInfo to etcd under its own
// lease. ClusterService surfaces that membership view + the local
// inventory + the desired-spec object counts as one hierarchical
// envelope. Lease loss (process crash / network partition) auto-removes
// the peer within 1 lease TTL (default 8s).
//
// Determinism
// -----------
// Every list in the response (cluster.nodes, appliances, dpus, enis)
// is sorted by stable key so two back-to-back GetTopology calls on
// identical inputs return byte-identical bodies. Clients can compute
// reliable diffs.
//
// Cost model
// ----------
// GetTopology is a pure-CPU pass over local in-memory maps; no etcd
// reads, no per-request fan-out. Sub-millisecond at typical scale
// (≤ 100 DPUs).

